The first version of the spec wrongly claimed the Rigveda Śākala Pada-pāṭha
didn't exist — it does, as the accented pada_patha field already on all
10,552 mantras (checked directly, confirmed against dge/veda_toolkit/README.md).
Also replaces the single unverified archive.org PDF citation for the
Prātiśākhya sūtra text with a three-layer sourcing plan verified live:
Sanskrit Library's TEI/XML edition (Scharf 2010, CC BY-NC-SA 3.0) as the
canonical machine-readable base, VedaViṣṭāram (Uvaṭa Bhāṣya + Viṣṇumitra
Vṛtti) and the RV-Prātiśākhya project as cross-checks, plus a concrete
per-paṭala rule-database file layout and schema. Also corrects the earlier
draft's suggestion to use a Vedic Extensions codepoint for dīrgha-svarita
without checking it against the font-support trap this repo already hit
and fixed for svarita/anudātta. PENDING.md updated to match.

